# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/.vinext/
/out/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
/dist/
/.wrangler/
/outputs/

# Everything written for an assistant rather than for the project: the running
# notes in ai/NOTES.md, the standing instructions in ai/README.md, and whatever
# one-off probes and scratch files a session leaves behind. None of it is
# reviewed, none of it should be, and it carries absolute paths and dates from
# whichever machine it was written on.
#
# What belongs in the repository instead: anything true about the *project*
# rather than about the work of changing it. Put that in a comment beside the
# code, which is where the next reader will be standing.
/ai/

# Editor and assistant scaffolding. Same argument as `/ai/` above: these describe
# the work of changing the project rather than the project, they are written by
# whichever tool happened to be open, and none of it is reviewed.
/.claude/
/.abacusai/
